course: dictionary
lesson: 1696
title: Slang from Down Under
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Slang is informal, everyday talk that people use with friends. Some slang belongs to one country or region, so people elsewhere may not know it. Context helps: «"Chunder" is Australian slang for vomit.» The sentence says it is slang and gives the meaning straight away.
explain: Chunder is a rough, jokey word, so it is never polite. You would not use it in a formal letter or in front of a head teacher. People might use it about a rough boat trip or when someone is ill. Because it is rude, check with a grown-up before you use slang you hear somewhere new.
fact: Slang is informal talk, and it is not usually found in formal writing.
fact: «Chunder» means to vomit, which means to be sick.
fact: As a verb, «chunder» is the act of being sick; as a noun, «chunder» is the vomit itself.
fact: Chunder is used in Australia and New Zealand, and it is known in the UK too.
fact: Chunder is never polite, so keep it for chatting with friends, not for school work.
exercise: «"Chunder" is Australian slang for vomit.» Where is chunder mostly used? | Only in the United States | *Australia and New Zealand, and known in the UK | Only in Scotland | In every school in the world
exercise: «The boat rocked so badly that Sam had to chunder over the side.» What does chunder mean here? | *To be sick | To sing loudly | To fall asleep | To swim fast
exercise: Why should you not use chunder in a formal letter? | Because it is a very long word | Because it is only used by teachers | *Because it is rough, jokey slang and not polite | Because it means something kind
test: «The deck was covered in chunder.» What kind of word is chunder here? | Verb, to be sick | Adverb, slowly | Adjective, very loud | *Noun, the vomit itself
test: «Yesterday, Max ___ all over the car seat.» Which form fits the gap? | *chundered | chunders | chunder | chundering
exam: What is the best meaning of chunder? | A loud noise made by a boat | *To be sick, or the vomit itself | A kind word for a friend | Feeling very tired after a long walk
